  "aiContextParagraph": "Indonesia is currently experiencing widespread flooding across several provinces following persistent heavy rainfall. In West Java, the overflow of the Citarum River has submerged parts of Dayeuhkolot, affecting nearly 20,000 people, while urban areas in Jakarta, such as Muara Angke and Cakung, have seen rising tidal waters and street flooding. Conditions remain critical in Sumatra, where regions in Aceh, including Aceh Singkil and Subulussalam, have faced prolonged inundation for over a week. Similar reports of displacement and property damage have emerged from West Sumatra and other parts of the archipelago. Local disaster mitigation agencies and police units are actively conducting evacuation efforts and providing emergency support to help affected citizens navigate daily activities and commute to schools amidst the rising water levels.",
